    "Coverage is partial: central calendar API was inaccessible, several daily pages and the Libraries calendar returned HTTP 429, and CampusGroups/Late Night could not be retrieved. Missing listings do not mean there are no events.",
    "Eastman’s own calendar and direct concert pages supplied the music listings. Student-only masterclasses are omitted. One central-calendar jazz listing names a different guest; Eastman’s own current page identifies Mike Moreno.",
    "Official football, field hockey, men’s/women’s soccer and swimming sources supplied the sports listed. Soccer times have been converted from Central to Eastern. Volleyball timed out; rowing, cross-country, tennis, golf, squash and remaining varsity schedules were not fully verified in this rapid pass.",
    "Economics workshop index and Wallis’s current schedule were checked; standing weekly workshop times were not treated as confirmed events. Individual Economics workshop pages still need a complete pass. Wallis has no dated seminar in this window on its published table.",
    "Arthur Satz Music lists October 18 and November 1 concerts, with none dated in this window. Humanities, Theatre, Dance and Simon pages were checked, but dynamic source completeness is not established. The dance opening was verified on its original event page. The Goergen events URL was inaccessible; Computer Science talks were recovered separately.",
    "Computer Science’s department listing displays 4 PM for the Du and Tang talks while direct Localist event pages explicitly show noon Eastern. The digest uses the direct event pages and flags the discrepancy.",
    "Plutzik and Kafka reading dates/times were found in indexed official event listings; their rooms could not be verified. These entries explicitly flag that limitation. Full calendar pagination and comprehensive source coverage are not certified."
